WEBVTT

00:01.020 --> 00:03.250
<b>I get it!</b>

00:03.350 --> 00:04.750
<b>It's hard to get.</b>

00:04.860 --> 00:07.980
<b>Yes, it sure is romantic.</b>

00:15.370 --> 00:19.500
<b>Usada's parents do appear
a couple of times after this.</b>

00:19.600 --> 00:21.040
<b>Yes they do.</b>

00:22.410 --> 00:24.170
<b>But we don't know what they do.</b>

00:25.010 --> 00:28.070
<b>All we know is they're going to
break down the trade barriers</b>

00:28.180 --> 00:30.770
<b>between the U.S. and Japan
and they're on a raft.</b>

00:30.880 --> 00:32.870
<b>To get to the U.S.</b>

00:35.550 --> 00:38.550
<b>I just want to make it clear
to the U.S. fans,</b>

00:38.660 --> 00:44.420
<b>it's impossible to go from Japan
to the U.S. on a raft.</b>

00:52.670 --> 00:54.930
<b>Oh, there's the ''space'' again.</b>

00:55.040 --> 00:59.030
<b>Note: night time store -
red light district shop</b>

00:55.040 --> 00:59.030
<b>When you look at this,
it's almost like a ''night time store.''</b>

01:06.250 --> 01:09.150
<b>I don't know if Americans know
what melon bread is.</b>

01:11.760 --> 01:14.160
<b>We don't have anything
called ''melon bread.''</b>

01:14.260 --> 01:16.560
<b>And it's not even
melon flavored, is it?</b>

01:16.660 --> 01:21.390
<b>There are some melon bread
that are melon flavored these days.</b>

01:25.470 --> 01:31.310
<b>The bread generally has a biscuit
on the outside,</b>

01:31.410 --> 01:37.680
<b>and it has marks similar
to musk melons.</b>

01:38.820 --> 01:44.250
<b>That's where the name comes from.</b>

01:44.760 --> 01:48.850
<b>It's really popular
in Japan right now.</b>

01:49.260 --> 01:53.320
<b>This anime is 4 years old, but people
line up now to buy the bread.</b>

01:53.430 --> 01:55.090
<b>We were ahead of the times.</b>

01:55.200 --> 01:57.330
<b>Even without knowing it.</b>

01:59.300 --> 02:01.170
<b>It's really popular now.</b>

02:02.010 --> 02:06.710
<b>There are a lot of stories
about aching stomachs.</b>

02:06.810 --> 02:09.370
<b>Does director Sakurai like
those types of topics?</b>

02:09.480 --> 02:10.850
<b>I believe he does.</b>

02:10.950 --> 02:14.210
<b>It looks like it. Tummy aches...</b>

02:15.820 --> 02:16.950
<b>Burps...</b>

02:17.220 --> 02:20.450
<b>How do Americans feel about this?</b>

02:22.060 --> 02:27.590
<b>It's called bathroom humor.</b>

02:29.270 --> 02:31.360
<b>I like Puchiko's line there.</b>

02:31.470 --> 02:34.530
<b>So it's accepted?</b>

02:35.540 --> 02:39.530
<b>It's not something that
would be disgusting?</b>

02:40.010 --> 02:43.280
<b>It might be,</b>

02:43.380 --> 02:49.320
<b>but that's the appeal
of Di Gi Charat.</b>

02:50.690 --> 02:52.710
<b>They're so forgiving.</b>

03:24.190 --> 03:29.820
<b>We made a product called
Deji-Candy.</b>

03:30.400 --> 03:35.420
<b>Just like the anime,
it was inside of a can like that.</b>

03:37.470 --> 03:39.160
<b>So they were advertising for us.</b>

03:39.270 --> 03:41.030
<b>Yes, we're very thankful.</b>

03:41.140 --> 03:43.770
<b>There's a lot of product placement.</b>
